---
// Figure 2 of the Health Dashboard case study: one example night planned backward from an
// exam, from 9 p.m. to the exam at 9 a.m. Example values only. Goes inside Figure, which
// styles the classes.
---
<svg
  viewBox="0 0 600 112"
  role="img"
  aria-label="Example: for a 9 a.m. exam the wake-up is 7:30 a.m.; 8 hours of sleep plus 15 minutes to fall asleep puts bedtime at 11:15 p.m."
>
  <line class="ax" x1="20" x2="580" y1="60" y2="60"></line>
  <rect class="settle" x="116.9" y="44" width="10.8" height="32" rx="2"></rect>
  <rect class="sleep" x="127.7" y="44" width="344.6" height="32" rx="3"></rect>
  <text class="on" x="300" y="65" text-anchor="middle">8 hours of sleep</text>
  <line class="tick" x1="116.9" x2="116.9" y1="36" y2="84"></line>
  <line class="tick" x1="472.3" x2="472.3" y1="36" y2="84"></line>
  <line class="tick" x1="149.2" x2="149.2" y1="78" y2="84"></line>
  <rect class="exam" x="531" y="50" width="12" height="20" rx="2"></rect>
  <text class="lb" x="116.9" y="26" text-anchor="middle">In bed 11:15 p.m.</text>
  <text class="lb" x="472.3" y="26" text-anchor="middle">Wake-up 7:30 a.m.</text>
  <text class="num" x="537" y="98" text-anchor="middle">Exam 9 a.m.</text>
  <text class="num" x="20" y="98">9 p.m.</text>
  <text x="149.2" y="98" text-anchor="middle">Midnight</text>
</svg>
